{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And the section of the female cult prostitute is juxtaposed to [the section of] the slave. And the transmitters of the religion said that <b>the holy one</b> is the one who is lain with, and the evidence is <b>from his being associated with beasts</b>, as in <b>נפשם כנגד חיתם</b>. And Elihu said, <b>וחיתם בקדשים</b>. And here it is written, <b>וגם קדש היה בארץ</b>; <b>בתי הקדשים</b>, where it is written <b>אשר הנשים אורגות שם</b>. Now I do not understand the meaning of <b>qedesha</b> [female cult prostitute]. But when one investigates the meaning of the word thoroughly, it is known that it is prepared for every passerby. And the evidence — where is <b>the qedesha</b>? If so, <b>qadesh</b> would be like the practice of the Egyptians, and the discerning will understand. And on account of <b>qedesha</b> the section of <b>the fee of a prostitute</b> is juxtaposed."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:34.490935600Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}